  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, state law cannot require generic drugs to use different warnings because Hatch\u2011Waxman mandates identical warnings to those on the brand\u2011name product."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, a claim that a generic manufacturer is liable for not requesting a label change is pre\u2011empted by Buckman, since disclosure obligations are federal in nature."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, generic manufacturers have a formal statutory and regulatory duty to revise labeling when there is reasonable evidence of a serious hazard."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, the Buckman case was against a consultant, not the manufacturer, supporting the view that manufacturer liability is pre\u2011empted."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Lefkowitz",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Lefkowitz, the FDA has never said that a generic drug using the brand label required by 505(j) is misbranded."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners' Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "United States",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 44,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States, the Hatch\u2011Waxman amendments do not relieve manufacturers of post\u2011approval safety responsibilities, including maintaining an adequate label."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bograd",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0021"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bograd, state law imposes an obligation to provide a warning and to go to the FDA to request a stronger warning; failure to do so could give rise to liability unless pre\u2011empted."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 2,
                "start": 2
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States (amicus curiae), according to United States (amicus curiae), the United States, as amicus curiae, supports the respondents\u2019 view that generic manufacturers may have obligations under federal law."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondents' Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
